WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.042
Before learners arrive, open the
starter directly in VS Code.

00:00:04.042 --> 00:00:35.708
Stage a small session with a decision
and a follow-up.

00:00:35.708 --> 00:00:44.833
Ask the room to predict what the next
developer would need; return to their

00:00:44.833 --> 00:00:47.458
answers at the end.

00:00:47.458 --> 00:00:54.292
Use the first eight minutes for three
checks: the workspace root, a current

00:00:54.292 --> 00:00:57.458
Node runtime and a passing suite.

00:00:57.458 --> 00:01:14.833
Select Agent mode and a frontier model.

00:01:14.833 --> 00:01:27.833
Distribute the five connection values
privately, not in the projected chat.

00:01:27.833 --> 00:01:31.458
In the next seventeen minutes, project
the customizations view.

00:01:31.458 --> 00:01:35.208
Ask someone to identify the one role
that should appear in the chat picker.

00:01:35.208 --> 00:02:13.458
Then show why the lead has an agent
tool but no edit or execute permission.

00:02:13.458 --> 00:02:18.792
If the team does not appear, check
which folder VS Code opened and inspect

00:02:18.792 --> 00:02:19.917
the frontmatter warnings.

00:02:19.917 --> 00:02:24.708
If a security worker proposes a patch,
ask who actually has permission to

00:02:24.708 --> 00:02:25.083
edit.

00:02:25.083 --> 00:02:29.667
The reviewer should return a finding
with a file and line.

00:02:29.667 --> 00:02:36.417
For lab two, reserve ten of fifteen
minutes for skill creation, three for

00:02:36.417 --> 00:02:39.042
attachment and two for discovery.

00:02:39.042 --> 00:02:43.417
Ask: if we replace the docs playbook,
can the writer suddenly run a terminal?

00:02:43.417 --> 00:02:51.292
No.

00:02:51.292 --> 00:02:53.458
Permissions belong to the agent.

00:02:53.458 --> 00:02:57.625
A missing skill usually warrants a
spelling check before another

00:02:57.625 --> 00:02:58.458
generation attempt.

00:02:58.458 --> 00:03:44.375
Compare the directory, frontmatter name
and worker reference side by side.

00:03:44.375 --> 00:03:48.583
Have everyone switch to Chronicle
Orchestrator before dispatching the

00:03:48.583 --> 00:03:49.542
first feature.

00:03:49.542 --> 00:03:54.625
In lab three, allow ten minutes for
implementation and five for the live

00:03:54.625 --> 00:03:55.000
test.

00:03:55.000 --> 00:03:59.917
Project the fixture dialog for
orientation, then blank the projector

00:03:59.917 --> 00:04:01.417
for real entry.

00:04:01.417 --> 00:04:05.625
Ask learners what the public settings
endpoint should reveal about the

00:04:05.625 --> 00:04:07.542
secret: only whether it exists.

00:04:07.542 --> 00:04:12.792
If token acquisition fails, check the
tenant, client and secret privately.

00:04:12.792 --> 00:04:17.875
If the token succeeds but Foundry
forbids the call, check the project

00:04:17.875 --> 00:04:20.417
target and Foundry Agent Consumer
assignment.

00:04:20.417 --> 00:04:30.417
Timebox the detour; label a mock-only
result honestly.

00:04:30.417 --> 00:04:34.875
In the eighteen-minute handoff lab,
have a learner choose a session they

00:04:34.875 --> 00:04:36.250
are permitted to send.

00:04:36.250 --> 00:04:43.292
Ask for one known fact and one open
task before clicking Create session

00:04:43.292 --> 00:04:43.833
summary.

00:04:43.833 --> 00:04:47.292
Those are your acceptance criteria, not
the word count.

00:04:47.292 --> 00:05:39.792
Demonstrate the multi-chunk path with a
deterministic test.

00:05:39.792 --> 00:05:52.792
The expected calls are a digest for
each part and one final synthesis.

00:05:52.792 --> 00:05:56.250
Ask why a short session skips the extra
round trips.

00:05:56.250 --> 00:05:59.208
Keep the live example small enough to
finish.

00:05:59.208 --> 00:06:51.750
Show how the log differs from the
Markdown output.

00:06:51.750 --> 00:06:55.625
If the popup is blocked, use the inline
fallback.

00:06:55.625 --> 00:07:01.083
If a job fails, inspect its last phase
rather than rerunning blindly.

00:07:01.083 --> 00:07:05.667
Never ask someone to paste a token or a
raw credential file.

00:07:05.667 --> 00:07:11.292
In lab five, let the tester draft
checks while the developer renders the

00:07:11.292 --> 00:07:14.750
icon, but run them after the asset
lands.

00:07:14.750 --> 00:07:18.750
If time slips, cut the desktop tour to
one diagram.

00:07:18.750 --> 00:07:23.375
Do not skip the direct PNG request or
the regression suite.

00:07:23.375 --> 00:07:28.208
For the closing recap, ask where the
desktop server would run, where its

00:07:28.208 --> 00:07:30.833
credentials would live, and what ships
today.

00:07:30.833 --> 00:07:36.167
The answers are a separate utility
process, writable per-user storage

00:07:36.167 --> 00:07:40.542
outside the installer, and the
package-free browser release.
